   "display_name": "Days In Month",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Write a function <code>days_in_month(month, year)</code> that takes a month (an integer from 1 to 12, where 1 is January) and a year (a positive integer, int &gt; 0), and <b>returns</b> how many days that month has in that year:</p>\n<ul><li>April (4), June (6), September (9) and November (11) have <b>30</b> days.</li><li>February (2) has <b>29</b> days in a leap year, and <b>28</b> days otherwise.</li><li>All other months have <b>31</b> days.</li></ul>\n<p><b>Leap year rule:</b> the year must be divisible by 4, and if the year is also divisible by 100, then it is a leap year only if it is also divisible by 400. For example, 2024 and 2000 are leap years, but 2023 and 1900 are not.</p>\n<p><b>Examples:</b> <code>days_in_month(1, 2025)</code> returns <code>31</code>. <code>days_in_month(4, 2025)</code> returns <code>30</code>. <code>days_in_month(2, 2024)</code> returns <code>29</code>. <code>days_in_month(2, 1900)</code> returns <code>28</code>.</p>",
