   "xml_index": 6,
   "xml_name": "PS5_006_Function Armstrong Number",
   "display_name": "Armstrong Number",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>A three-digit number is an <b>Armstrong number</b> if the sum of the <b>cubes</b> of its digits is equal to the number itself. For example, 153 is an Armstrong number, because 1 * 1 * 1 + 5 * 5 * 5 + 3 * 3 * 3 = 1 + 125 + 27 = 153.</p>\n<p>Write a function <code>is_armstrong(n)</code> that takes a three-digit positive integer <code>n</code> (from 100 to 999) and <b>returns</b> <code>True</code> if it is an Armstrong number, or <code>False</code> otherwise.</p>\n<p><b>Examples:</b> <code>is_armstrong(153)</code> returns <code>True</code>. <code>is_armstrong(370)</code> returns <code>True</code>. <code>is_armstrong(100)</code> returns <code>False</code>.</p>",
