   "display_name": "Remove Vowels",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Write a function <code>remove_vowels(text)</code> that takes a string <code>text</code> of lowercase letters and spaces, and <b>returns</b> a new string with all the vowels (<code>a</code>, <code>e</code>, <code>i</code>, <code>o</code>, <code>u</code>) removed. Everything else (including spaces) stays, in the same order.</p>\n<p><b>Python facts you may use:</b> <code>for ch in text:</code> goes through the characters of a string one by one, and <code>+</code> joins two strings: <code>\"ab\" + \"c\"</code> is <code>\"abc\"</code>. An empty string is written <code>\"\"</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Examples:</b> <code>remove_vowels(\"hello world\")</code> returns <code>\"hll wrld\"</code>. <code>remove_vowels(\"rhythm\")</code> returns <code>\"rhythm\"</code>. <code>remove_vowels(\"aeiou\")</code> returns <code>\"\"</code>.</p>",
