   "xml_name": "PS5_013_Function Count Above Average",
   "display_name": "Count Above Average",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Write a function <code>count_above_average(lst)</code> that takes a non-empty list of integers <code>lst</code> and <b>returns</b> how many elements are <b>greater than</b> the average of the list. (The average is the sum of the elements divided by how many there are.)</p>\n<p><b>Python facts you may use:</b> <code>len(lst)</code> gives the number of elements in a list, and <code>lst[i]</code> gives the element at position <code>i</code> (positions start from 0, so the last position is <code>len(lst) - 1</code>).</p>\n<p><b>Examples:</b> <code>count_above_average([1, 2, 3, 4])</code> returns <code>2</code> (the average is 2.5, and 3 and 4 are above it). <code>count_above_average([5, 5, 5])</code> returns <code>0</code>. <code>count_above_average([-3, 0, 9])</code> returns <code>1</code>.</p>",
