   "xml_name": "PS5_018_Recursive Integer Division",
   "display_name": "Recursive Integer Division",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Division is repeated subtraction: 17 divided by 5 is 3 (with 2 left over), because you can take 5 away from 17 three times before less than 5 is left.</p>\n<p>Write a recursive function <code>int_divide(a, b)</code> that takes a non-negative integer (int &gt;= 0) <code>a</code> and a positive integer (int &gt; 0) <code>b</code>, and <b>returns</b> <code>a // b</code>, <b>without</b> using <code>//</code>, <code>/</code> or <code>%</code>.</p>\n<p>Your function <b>must be recursive</b> (it must call itself), and must <b>not</b> use any loop.</p>\n<p><b>Examples:</b> <code>int_divide(17, 5)</code> returns <code>3</code>. <code>int_divide(4, 5)</code> returns <code>0</code>. <code>int_divide(0, 3)</code> returns <code>0</code>. <code>int_divide(20, 4)</code> returns <code>5</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "print(int_divide(17, 5))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "3",
