   "xml_name": "PS5_020_Recursive Count Character",
   "display_name": "Recursive Count Character",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Write a recursive function <code>count_char(text, ch, index)</code> that takes a string <code>text</code>, a single character <code>ch</code>, and a position <code>index</code> (where <code>0 &lt;= index &lt;= len(text)</code>), and <b>returns</b> how many times <code>ch</code> appears in <code>text</code> from position <code>index</code> up to the end.</p>\n<p>Your function <b>must be recursive</b> (it must call itself), and must <b>not</b> use any loop.</p>\n<p><b>Python facts you may use:</b> <code>len(text)</code> gives the number of characters in a string, and <code>text[i]</code> gives the character at position <code>i</code> (positions start from 0).</p>\n<p><b>Examples:</b> <code>count_char(\"banana\", \"a\", 0)</code> returns <code>3</code>. <code>count_char(\"banana\", \"a\", 4)</code> returns <code>1</code>. <code>count_char(\"banana\", \"z\", 0)</code> returns <code>0</code>. <code>count_char(\"\", \"a\", 0)</code> returns <code>0</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "print(count_char(\"banana\", \"a\", 0))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "3",
